  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Action-based learning for Narrative Power project stimulates learning and innovation on narrative approaches through pilots in three countries. The pilots aim to shift harmful narratives related to shrinking civic space in their particular context. In Tunisia, the project will support diverse civil society partners to strengthen their narrative capacities and develop a narrative-based campaign strategy, building on their newly developed toolkit on hope-based narratives. In El Salvador, the project will convene spaces for youth to develop and disseminate alternative narratives on civic space and climate justice. In Myanmar, the project will supporta partner organization to adopt creative dissemination strategies for rights-based narratives.  The experiences from the country pilots will support learning on narrative approaches across the confederation, especially around alliance building for narrative power, innovative approaches to disseminate narratives, and measuring narrative change.
Through the project, Oxfam in El Salvador will work together with the local partner Plataforma Global to organize a Narratives Laboratory on Inequalities and Rights. The lab will involve youth activists to co-design a narratives-based campaign to position problems and solutions regarding inequalities in contextsof closed civic space. The project will systematize good practices and knowledge learned from the experience.</narrative>
  </description>
